    },
    "description": "Contoso deploys the same Tenant Portal at several sites. One site uses LDAP with password authentication, another uses Kerberos tickets, and a cloud region accepts OIDC tokens; a local emergency deployment uses a database-backed password check. The Login Controller currently branches among these checks and different callers also duplicate lockout, error translation, and audit behavior. The new design needs a deployment-configured component registry that selects a verifier by tenant and channel without changing the controller or domain code. Each verifier must report either one normalized successful identity, including the directory identity and verified attributes, or an explicit reason such as expired evidence, unavailable provider, or rejected credential. Password-specific throttling must remain inside the password verification path and must not disable Kerberos or federated logins. The Login Controller must not import LDAP, Kerberos, OIDC, or database-verification APIs, and adding a fourth mechanism must require only a new implementation plus deployment configuration. Verification failures must be audited without logging secrets or complete tokens.",
    "decision_statement": "Decide whether to isolate mechanism-specific credential checks behind a deployment-selected verification boundary that returns a uniform success or explicit failure to the login workflow.",
    "notes": "A deployment-configured verifier registry behind one uniform success/failure boundary (authenticator) is the decision; subject-descriptor is the near-miss via the normalized successful identity each verifier returns."
  },
